# Secrets. Nothing matched here may ever be committed.
#
# The device's TLS material and the APNs signing key are the two things that
# would let someone else impersonate this deployment, so the patterns are
# deliberately broad: it is cheaper to force an explicit `git add -f` for a
# harmless file than to leak a private key once.
.env
secrets/
*.p8
*.key
*.pem
*.der
*.crt
*.csr
*.srl
aes.key

# Hello's build output. suripu-app-*.jar is 77 MB and is not ours to
# redistribute; it is supplied at build time through the `jars` build context.
# See README.md, "The suripu jar".
*.jar

# Compiled output from the source trees in this repository. All of it is
# reproducible with `make build`, and orb/migrate in particular is a stale
# 13 MB binary from before cmd/migrate was a one-shot tool.
orb-algo/build/
orb/migrate
orb/orb
orb/apidiff
orb/compare
orb/pushsend
orb/timecheck

# 25 MB of DynamoDB scan output holding REAL SLEEP DATA, read by cmd/migrate as
# a fixed snapshot. It is data, not source, and there is a verified copy in the
# backups directory. It must never be committed.
orb/migrations/dump/

# Backups and database dumps. These contain real sleep data.
backups/
dump/
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*.tar.gz

# Local-only compose overrides.
docker-compose.override.yml
*.local.yml

.DS_Store

# The repository root ignores *_pb2.py as generated code, which is usually
# right. This one is a BUILD INPUT: sense-server/Dockerfile COPYs it, so
# without this un-ignore the Linux sense-server image fails to build for
# anyone who clones. Regenerate it from ntp.proto if you would rather not
# carry generated code.
!sense-server/ntp_pb2.py
